{"id":"u-01979ccf-2b60-4758-a865-d61a6110566d","src":"community","title":"Minimalist Upper Body V-Shape","author":"DjungelJarl","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/tabIYR-untitled-program","desc":"A time-efficient, 3-day upper-body program built for the V-taper look: wider shoulders, wider lats and a smaller-looking waist. It's designed for 80/20 results meaning you get most of the gains of a full program in about 35–45 minutes per session, and it works well while you're in a calorie deficit.\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\n- Lifters who want broader shoulders and a stronger V-shape, especially if wide hips or a blocky waist frame is something you'd like to offset\n- Anyone cutting fat who wants to keep and build upper-body muscle without living in the gym\nBeginner to intermediate lifters. You don't need to be able to do pull-ups yet, since the program builds them.\n\nSCHEDULE\n3 days per week on non-consecutive days (for example Mon, Wed, Fri). Each day trains lats and side delts, the two muscles that matter most for width.\nDay A: Width. Chin-ups, wide pulldowns, shoulder press, lateral raises, face pulls, arms.\nDay B: Strength. Chin-ups and negatives, dips, rows, lateral raises with a drop set, optional Romanian deadlift.\nDay C: Shoulders and detail. Pulldowns, incline press, lateral raises, rear-delt flyes, arms.\n\nEFFORT (RPE)\nRPE is how hard a set is: RPE 8 means you could do 2 more clean reps, RPE 9 means 1 more, and RPE 10 means you hit failure. Compound lifts stay at RPE 8–9 to keep form clean and joints happy. Isolation lifts like lateral raises go to RPE 9–10. Effort usually rises across sets, so expect your last set to feel the hardest.\n\nPROGRESSION\nUse double progression. When you hit the top of the rep range on every set, add weight next session and start back at the bottom of the range. If you're dieting, holding your strength steady is a win.\n\nCHIN-UP PROGRESSION\nStart with low reps and perfect form: a full hang and chin over the bar on every rep. Each week, add 1 rep to one set. Once you can do 4 sets of 5, switch to 3 sets of 5–8 and drop the negatives. At 3 sets of 8, start adding weight or move on to pull-ups.\n\nDELOAD\nWeeks 1–5 are normal training. In week 6, keep the same weights but cut your sets in half. Then start a new block.\n\nTIPS\nLateral raises are the stars of this program. Use light weights, strict form and cables when you can.\nDips: stop when your upper arms are parallel to the floor. Swap to incline dumbbell press if your shoulders complain.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-30T06:30:20.410Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Width","Strength","Shoulders and detail"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Chin-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":2,"hi":3,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":120},{"ss":[{"n":"Wide Grip Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":60},{"n":"Seated Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":60}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"rest":60},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":9,"x":2}],"rest":45},{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":2}],"rest":60},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":2}],"rest":60}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Chin-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":2,"hi":4,"rpe":9,"x":4}],"rest":120},{"n":"Chin-up (Negatives)","sets":[{"r":3,"rpe":9,"x":2}],"rest":120},{"n":"Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":90},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":90},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"x":3},{"lo":12,"hi":20,"rpe":10}],"note":"Last set dropset","rest":120}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"rest":